Package: mchaid
Type: Package
Title: Chi-Square and F Automatic Interaction Detection (CHAID, AID) Trees
Version: 0.9.5
Date: 2026-11-22
Authors@R: c(person("Modesto", "Escobar", email = "modesto@usal.es", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("MICIU/AEI", role = "fnd",
    comment = "Grants CSO2013-49278-EXP, PGC2018-093755-B-I00, PDC2022-133355-I00, PID2023-147358NB-I00 funded by MICIU/AEI/10.13039/501100011033 and by European Union NextGenerationEU/PRTR"))
Description: Grows CHAID decision trees (Kass, 1980) for a categorical or
    ordinal response, and the equivalent trees with F tests for a
    quantitative response, with ordered and unordered categorical predictors,
    including exhaustive CHAID (Biggs, de Ville and Suen, 1991), a floating
    category for missing values, frequency weights and Bonferroni-adjusted
    splitting tests. The tests are likelihood-ratio tests computed from
    cross-tabulations, so no package other than those distributed with R is
    needed. The package is a port of the Stata commands 'mchaid' and 'maid',
    which are based on the Stata command 'chaid' by Joseph N. Luchman. It
    provides print, summary, plot (tree drawn with base graphics, in two styles: the
    classic one and one with a box for every node, with bars or box plots), predict,
    a classification table, a permutation importance of the predictors, a
    conversion of the tree to a network of the 'netCoin' package and an
    interactive version of the tree as an HTML page.
License: GPL-3
